FYDE: drm/v3d: add system suspend/resume support

The V3D driver had no PM ops at all, so nothing re-initialised the GPU
across a system suspend/resume. On V3D >= 7.1 (Pi5) the power island is
managed by the SMS state machine; after resume it is left powered off,
so the first hang-recovery reset spins in v3d_reset_sms() and prints
"Failed to wait for SMS reset", leaving the GPU permanently wedged. The
compositor then hangs and the hardware watchdog (bcm2835-wdt, pet by
daisydog) warm-resets the board -- observed as a reboot loop, and
reproducible on demand with `powerd_dbus_suspend`.

Add .suspend/.resume callbacks that mirror probe's hardware bring-up:

  suspend: v3d_irq_disable() -> v3d_power_off_sms() -> clk_disable_unprepare()
  resume:  clk_prepare_enable() -> v3d_idle_sms() (power the SMS back up
           FIRST) -> v3d_init_hw_state() -> v3d_mmu_set_page_table() ->
           v3d_irq_reset() -> restore clk_down_rate

v3d_init_hw_state() is un-staticed and prototyped so the resume path can
reprogram the core.

Software state (queues, page table allocation, scheduler) persists across
suspend, so only the hardware is reprogrammed. Any GPU job still in flight
at suspend time is recovered by the scheduler timeout after resume.

This complements 041-fix-kernel-warning-in-suspending.patch, which fixed
the pl011/rp1/dwc3/macb/vc4_hdmi resume paths but did not cover v3d.

BUG=none
TEST=emerge-rpi5-openfyde sys-kernel/raspberry-kernel; powerd_dbus_suspend on device
